        "original_id": "d80c41e4-5031-549c-8cac-be1b5a1bbeb0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Nottingham, England\n- Transport stops: Royal Centre tram stop, Nottingham Trent University tram stop\n- Organizations: Nottingham Trent University\n- Buildings and venues: Cornerhouse, Victoria Centre, Newton Building, Arkwright Building\n- Products and artworks: Aqua Horological Tintinnabulator, Victoria Centre Clock, Emett Clock, The Time Fountain\n- Topics: proximity of tram stops, shopping centre, clock landmark\n\nFacts:\n- Intu Victoria Centre is a shopping centre in Nottingham, England, constructed between 1967 and 1972.\n- The Aqua Horological Tintinnabulator, also known as the Victoria Centre Clock, the Emett Clock, and The Time Fountain, is a water-powered clock in Nottingham, England.\n- Royal Centre tram stop is close to the Cornerhouse, the Victoria Centre, and the Newton Building of Nottingham Trent University.\n- Much of Nottingham Trent University's City Campus is closer to Nottingham Trent University tram stop than to Royal Centre tram stop.\n- Nottingham Trent University tram stop is near the university's flagship Arkwright and Newton buildings to the south.\n- The Newton Building is closer to Royal Centre tram stop than to Nottingham Trent University tram stop.",
